From sean@conman.org Sat Jun 20 01:28:10 2020
From: sean@conman.org (Sean Conner)
Date: Fri, 19 Jun 2020 21:28:10 -0400
Subject: Some new tests in the Gemini Client Torture Test
Message-ID: <20200620012810.GO11281@brevard.conman.org>
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit
MIME-Version: 1.0
X-Orbital-Fox-Message-Number: 1811
X-Orbital-Fox-Url: https://lists.orbitalfox.eu/archives/gemini/2020/001811.html
X-Orbital-Fox-Message-Number-Source: html-message-id


  I just added 10 new tests to the Gemini Client Torture Test, tests 41
through 50.  They all test section 5.4.1 of the Gemini Specification (text
lines).  Each page contains a line that exceeds 8,500 bytes (yes, bytes, not
characters, although some of then exceed 8,500 characters, depends upon the
characters used).  A few mild spoilers:

