> by starting a new Dillo process.


The way I do it in Amfora is normalize each URL for the cache and display,
so that URLs like //example.com:1965/ and gemini://example.com/ aren't cached
twice. And redirects are never cached, although maybe it makes sense to do that
separately.

makeworld

