> replaced eleven years ago. I suggest to change the specification and,
> instead of using the actual RFC number, use the "BCP" reference which
> is stable. "BCP 47" pointed to RFC 4646 before and now to the current
> one, 5646.
>

Nice catch. I agree with this change.

But may be this is not the best place to talk about the specification?
>

It's good that you brought it up, thank you.

We are resisting big changes to the spec since it's close to finalized, but
this is along the line of "getting it right the first time" so this is good.

Here's the HTTPS URL to BCP 47: <https://tools.ietf.org/html/bcp47>
Anyone know if it's mirrored in Gemini?

